  "query_preview": "stretch of hot temperatures. Flow aloft initially will be \nmore zonal before transitioning more southwesterly as the ridge \nnudges back westward ever so slightly toward the weekend. Monsoonal \nmoisture is decreasing, but remains across the region today, highest \nacross Southwest Montana. Although upper level support isn't \nparticularly great, widely scattered showers and thunderstorms look \nto develop through the afternoon and evening, with a few persisting \ninto the overnight. \n\nMonsoonal moisture decreases further Friday as a drier zonal flow \naloft remains for another day. That said, lingering moisture still \nlooks to result in isolated showers and thunderstorms, mostly across \nSouthwest Montana. Breezy west winds and hot temperatures will \nresult in increased fire weather concerns over the plains Friday, \nparticularly near the Canadian border where precipitation recently \nhas been minimal. \n\nThe southwesterly flow aloft works back in this weekend as \ntemperatures peak across most areas. Additional round of primarily \nafternoon and evening widely scattered showers and thunderstorms \nwill be around, mostly across Southwest MT and vicinity. \n\nThat story more or less persists into next week. Hot temperatures \nremain with opportunities for widely scattered showers and \nthunderstorms most afternoons, primarily across Southwest MT and \nvicinity. Areas further north on the plains look to remain hot and \ndry over this timeframe. Anyone that has to be outside for any \nextended stretch over the upcoming week should prepare for plenty of \nhydration breaks in the shade. -AM",
